              <div class="reveal" style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
                <h2
                  style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.8rem; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--ink);">
                  Pure Exploration &amp; Wonder</h2>
                <p>
                  Built entirely around curiosity and <strong>Montessori principles</strong>, there are absolutely
                  <strong>no things to win and no puzzles to
                    solve</strong>. Kids simply pan across the landscape, explore the environment, and listen to the
                  authentic <strong>sounds of animals and nature</strong>. Tapping the magnifying glass reveals
                  beautifully illustrated cards filled with fascinating facts about each element.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="simple-gallery reveal" style="margin-top: 2.5rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
                <img src="/images/screenshots/phone/kidamame_discovery_screenshot_24.jpeg"
                  alt="The Alps biome in Kidamame Discovery with a brown bear, wolf, marmot, golden eagle, and young explorer."
                  loading="lazy" />
                <img src="/images/screenshots/phone/kidamame_discovery_screenshot_15.jpeg"
                  alt="Educational fact card about the African savannah in Kidamame Discovery." loading="lazy" />
                <img src="/images/screenshots/phone/kidamame_discovery_screenshot_22.jpeg"
                  alt="Australian Outback scene with a Kangaroo Crossing Sign educational card, red kangaroo, and scorpion."
                  loading="lazy" />
                <img src="/images/screenshots/phone/kidamame_discovery_screenshot_10.jpeg"
                  alt="The Amazon Rainforest biome with a jaguar, poison dart frogs, toucan, squirrel monkey, and young explorer."
                  loading="lazy" />
              </div>

              <div class="reveal" style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
                <h2
                  style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.8rem; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--ink);">
                  Interactive Animals, Plants &amp; Natural Phenomena</h2>
                <p>
                  The app features <strong>6 stunning scenes</strong>: the Alps, the African Savannah, the
                  Australian Outback, the Arctic, the Sonoran Desert, and the Amazon Rainforest. Each sensory-rich biome
                  contains <strong>20 or more interactive elements</strong> (animals, plants, and natural phenomena). We
                  focus on the "small wonders," showing how even the tiniest creatures hide big secrets. Tap the ostrich
                  to see its eggs fall, touch the volcano to trigger a spectacular eruption, or watch the glacier front
                  collapse into the sea! With over 120 interactive elements in total, there are <strong>about 400
                    fascinating facts</strong> waiting to be discovered!
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="simple-gallery reveal" style="margin-top: 2.5rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
                <img src="/images/screenshots/phone/kidamame_discovery_screenshot_40.jpeg"
                  alt="Interactive Discovery Journal tracking nature elements discovered across the Alps biome."
                  loading="lazy" />
                <img src="/images/screenshots/phone/kidamame_discovery_screenshot_34.jpeg"
                  alt="Northern Lights (Aurora Borealis) illustrated science card in the Arctic biome."
                  loading="lazy" />
                <img src="/images/screenshots/phone/kidamame_discovery_screenshot_9.jpeg"
                  alt="Amazon Rainforest river scene with a capybara, green anaconda, caiman, squirrel monkey, and blue-and-yellow macaw."
                  loading="lazy" />
                <img src="/images/screenshots/phone/kidamame_discovery_screenshot_39.jpeg"
                  alt="Discovery Journal in the Sonoran Desert showing Saguaro Cactus, Tumbleweed, and Weaver's Needle badges."
                  loading="lazy" />
              </div>

              <div class="reveal" style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
                <h2
                  style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.8rem; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--ink);">
                  Quality Time Together</h2>
                <p>
                  We designed Kidamame Discovery as a <strong>shared experience</strong>. The app shines when a child
                  plays alongside an adult, exploring the biomes together while the parent helps reading the fun facts
                  which, by the way, are
                  genuinely interesting for adults too! In line with the latest <strong>American Academy of Pediatrics
                    (AAP) recommendations</strong> on screen time, Kidamame is built to encourage co-viewing and
                  meaningful family interactions. Our ultimate aspiration is that this shared digital wonder will
                  inspire your family to step outside and discover the magic of the real world.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="simple-gallery reveal" style="margin-top: 2.5rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
                <img src="/images/screenshots/phone/kidamame_discovery_screenshot_30.jpeg"
                  alt="Illustrated botanical fact card comparing pine needles and spruce needles in the Alps."
                  loading="lazy" />
                <img src="/images/screenshots/phone/kidamame_discovery_screenshot_14.jpeg"
                  alt="The African Savannah biome at sunset featuring a lion, meerkat, baboon, zebra, cheetah, and giraffes near Mount Kilimanjaro."
                  loading="lazy" />
                <img src="/images/screenshots/phone/kidamame_discovery_screenshot_31.jpeg"
                  alt="The Arctic biome under the Northern Lights with a polar bear and cub, Arctic fox, puffin, and walrus."
                  loading="lazy" />
                <img src="/images/screenshots/phone/kidamame_discovery_screenshot_21.jpeg"
                  alt="Australian Outback scene with a Kangaroo Crossing Sign educational card, red kangaroo, and scorpion."
                  loading="lazy" />
              </div>

              <div class="reveal" style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
                <h2
                  style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.8rem; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--ink);">
                  100% Offline &amp; Perfect for Travel</h2>
                <p>
                  Whether you are on a long <strong>airplane flight</strong>, taking a family <strong>road
                    trip</strong>,
                  waiting at a restaurant, or relaxing outdoors with no cellular reception, Kidamame Discovery is always
                  ready to play. With all animations, animal sounds, and nature facts stored directly on your device,
                  there is zero buffering, zero data usage, and no need for Wi-Fi. Just calm, reliable wonder wherever
                  your family travels.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="simple-gallery reveal" style="margin-top: 2.5rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
                <img src="/images/screenshots/phone/kidamame_discovery_screenshot_17.jpeg"
                  alt="African Savannah ecosystem fact card showing a baobab tree." loading="lazy" />
                <img src="/images/screenshots/phone/kidamame_discovery_screenshot_23.jpeg"
                  alt="Australian Outback biome with a aquila audax card." loading="lazy" />
                <img src="/images/screenshots/phone/kidamame_discovery_screenshot_38.jpeg"
                  alt="Bald Eagle illustrated wildlife card in the Sonoran Desert biome." loading="lazy" />
                <img src="/images/screenshots/phone/kidamame_discovery_screenshot_7.jpeg"
                  alt="Amazon Rainforest geothermal boiling river fact card alongside a jaguar and blue poison dart frog."
                  loading="lazy" />
              </div>

              <div class="promise-block reveal"
                style="background: var(--amber-soft); padding: 3rem; border-radius: 20px; border: 1px solid rgba(245, 165, 42, 0.2); margin-top: 4rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
                <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1.2rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                  <div
                    style="width: 50px; height: 50px; flex-shrink: 0; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--amber); color: white; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: 1.4rem;">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-shield-halved"></i>
                  </div>
                  <h2
                    style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 1.8rem); line-height: 1.2; color: var(--ink); margin: 0;">
                    No ads. No tracking. No subscriptions.
                  </h2>
                </div>
                <p style="margin-bottom: 0;">
                  We know how hard it is to find digital spaces you can trust. That's why we created <strong>The
                    Kidamame Promise</strong>: our apps will never feature advertisements, hidden subscription fees, or
                  confusing in-game currencies. You can <strong>download and try the first biome for free</strong> and,
                  if your family loves
                  it, a <strong>single one-time purchase</strong> unlocks all 6 biomes forever, protected behind a
                  <strong>child-proof Parental Gate</strong> so kids can never make accidental purchases, with
                  <strong>Family Sharing</strong> supported. Furthermore,
                  <strong>we do not collect any personal data</strong> from your children (built with strict
                  <strong>COPPA &amp; GDPR-K privacy-by-design</strong>, zero accounts, and zero third-party trackers)
                  and the app <strong>plays
                    fully offline</strong>, giving you complete peace of mind.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="simple-gallery reveal" style="margin-top: 2.5rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
                <img src="/images/gallery/thumbs/08.webp" class="landscape"
                  alt="Panoramic view of the Alps biome in Kidamame Discovery featuring mountain wildlife and pine forests."
                  loading="lazy" />
              </div>

              <!-- FAQ SECTION -->
              <div class="faq-section reveal" style="margin-top: 4rem; margin-bottom: 4rem;">
                <h2
                  style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.8rem; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 2rem; text-align: center;">
                  Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

                <div class="faq-list" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem;">
                  <details name="discovery-faq"
                    style="background: white; border: 1.5px solid rgba(58, 158, 228, 0.15); border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.2rem 1.5rem; cursor: pointer;">
                    <summary
                      style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink); list-style: none; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;">
                      Does Kidamame Discovery have ads?
                      <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down" style="color: var(--blue); font-size: 0.9rem;"></i>
                    </summary>
                    <p style="margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 0;">
                      No. Kidamame Discovery is 100% ad-free. We believe children should be able to explore and learn in
                      a calm environment without interruptions, as advertisements ruin the quality and the flow of the
                      play experience.
                    </p>
                  </details>

                  <details name="discovery-faq"
                    style="background: white; border: 1.5px solid rgba(58, 158, 228, 0.15); border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.2rem 1.5rem; cursor: pointer;">
                    <summary
                      style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink); list-style: none; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;">
                      Do I need a subscription, and what is included in the free trial?
                      <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down" style="color: var(--blue); font-size: 0.9rem;"></i>
                    </summary>
                    <p style="margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 0;">
                      No subscriptions, ever. We offer a simple, transparent pricing model: you can download the app and
                      explore the first biome for free to see if it's right for your family. If you love it, a single
                      one-time purchase unlocks all 6 biomes and ~400 nature facts forever, with no recurring monthly
                      fees and Family Sharing supported across your family's devices.
                    </p>
                  </details>

                  <details name="discovery-faq"
                    style="background: white; border: 1.5px solid rgba(58, 158, 228, 0.15); border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.2rem 1.5rem; cursor: pointer;">
                    <summary
                      style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink); list-style: none; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;">
                      How are in-app purchases and children's privacy protected?
                      <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down" style="color: var(--blue); font-size: 0.9rem;"></i>
                    </summary>
                    <p style="margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 0;">
                      The one-time full-version unlock is protected behind a child-proof Parental Gate, ensuring young
                      children cannot accidentally trigger a purchase or leave the app. Kidamame Discovery requires no
                      user account, collects zero personal data, and contains no third-party analytics or behavioral
                      trackers.
                    </p>
                  </details>

                  <details name="discovery-faq"
                    style="background: white; border: 1.5px solid rgba(58, 158, 228, 0.15); border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.2rem 1.5rem; cursor: pointer;">
                    <summary
                      style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink); list-style: none; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;">
                      Can I share my purchase between iOS and Android devices?
                      <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down" style="color: var(--blue); font-size: 0.9rem;"></i>
                    </summary>
                    <p style="margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 0;">
                      Within the same ecosystem (Apple Family Sharing across iPhones and iPads, or Google Play Family
                      Library across Android devices), your purchase is shared automatically. However, sharing between
                      iOS and Android is not possible automatically because Apple and Google manage store purchases
                      separately, and for your privacy we do not ask you to create a Kidamame user account or store
                      personal data on external servers. If your family uses both iOS and Android and needs a hand, just
                      reach out to us at <a href="mailto:support@kidamame.com"
                        style="color: var(--blue); font-weight: 700; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px;">support@kidamame.com</a>
                      and we will gladly find a solution together!
                    </p>
                  </details>

                  <details name="discovery-faq"
                    style="background: white; border: 1.5px solid rgba(58, 158, 228, 0.15); border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.2rem 1.5rem; cursor: pointer;">
                    <summary
                      style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink); list-style: none; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;">
                      Is the app completely offline?
                      <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down" style="color: var(--blue); font-size: 0.9rem;"></i>
                    </summary>
                    <p style="margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 0;">
                      Yes! An internet connection is only needed at the time of purchase if you decide to unlock the
                      full app. After that, Kidamame Discovery does not require an internet connection to play. It's
                      truly offline, meaning no tracking, no personal data collection, and it's perfect for road trips
                      or
                      flights.
                    </p>
                  </details>

                  <details name="discovery-faq"
                    style="background: white; border: 1.5px solid rgba(58, 158, 228, 0.15); border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.2rem 1.5rem; cursor: pointer;">
                    <summary
                      style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink); list-style: none; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;">
                      How many hours of exploration are there?
                      <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down" style="color: var(--blue); font-size: 0.9rem;"></i>
                    </summary>
                    <p style="margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 0;">
                      Depending on the child's pace, playtime can range from 30 minutes if they just explore and listen
                      to the relaxing sounds, up to 90 minutes or more if they discover and read all the interesting
                      facts.
                    </p>
                  </details>

                  <details name="discovery-faq"
                    style="background: white; border: 1.5px solid rgba(58, 158, 228, 0.15); border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.2rem 1.5rem; cursor: pointer;">
                    <summary
                      style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink); list-style: none; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;">
                      Are there puzzles to solve or levels to unlock?
                      <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down" style="color: var(--blue); font-size: 0.9rem;"></i>
                    </summary>
                    <p style="margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 0;">
                      No. Kidamame is pure exploration and discovery in a Montessori style. It is designed to inspire
                      curiosity about our world and nature without any stressful goals, timers, or scoreboards.
                    </p>
                  </details>

                  <details name="discovery-faq"
                    style="background: white; border: 1.5px solid rgba(58, 158, 228, 0.15); border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.2rem 1.5rem; cursor: pointer;">
                    <summary
                      style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink); list-style: none; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;">
                      Do you plan to add more biomes or scenes?
                      <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down" style="color: var(--blue); font-size: 0.9rem;"></i>
                    </summary>
                    <p style="margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 0;">
                      We might add one or two scenes, but it's not guaranteed. Because our app is completely offline and
                      all content is included in your download, we have strict storage limits to keep the app size
                      manageable. It's possible we will release new biomes as separate "chapters" in new apps. Sign up
                      for our newsletter below to stay updated on future releases!
                    </p>
                  </details>

                  <details name="discovery-faq"
                    style="background: white; border: 1.5px solid rgba(58, 158, 228, 0.15); border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.2rem 1.5rem; cursor: pointer;">
                    <summary
                      style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink); list-style: none; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;">
                      What is the recommended age for the app?
                      <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down" style="color: var(--blue); font-size: 0.9rem;"></i>
                    </summary>
                    <p style="margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 0;">
                      Kidamame Discovery is designed for kids ages 4
                      and up, but it grows with them! Younger kids can explore with a parent who can read the facts to
                      them, while older children can delve into the details on their own. Actually, thanks to the
                      fascinating nature facts and the calm, relaxing atmosphere, the app is genuinely engaging for
                      adults too!
                    </p>
                  </details>

                  <details name="discovery-faq"
                    style="background: white; border: 1.5px solid rgba(58, 158, 228, 0.15); border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.2rem 1.5rem; cursor: pointer;">
                    <summary
                      style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink); list-style: none; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;">
                      Which languages are supported?
                      <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down" style="color: var(--blue); font-size: 0.9rem;"></i>
                    </summary>
                    <p style="margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 0;">
                      Kidamame Discovery is available in English, Italian, French, German, Spanish, and Portuguese.
                    </p>
                  </details>
                </div>
              </div>

